 ## QG-13 — Bounded Critic rounds and correction-only PASS follow-ups
 
-- **Batch budget:** each meaningful, predeclared delivery batch receives one full independent Critic review and up to three fresh correction-diff reviews, stopping earlier on genuine PASS. Four Critic calls total is the maximum; there is no full-review rerun. A singleton batch is reserved for a substantial independent delivery or urgent isolated risk, not each item's completion by default.
-- **Correction follow-ups:** each requires a new committed correction, current deterministic evidence and the exact range `immediately-previous-reviewed-commit..new-candidate`. Continue only to resolve that batch's findings and direct regressions from the correction; stop at PASS or after the third correction-diff review. This is no unlimited retry authorization and removes no runtime budget or course gate.
+- **Batch budget:** each meaningful, predeclared delivery batch receives one full independent Critic review, then fresh correction-diff reviews until genuine PASS or an explicit PO decision (D190: no round or correction-commit count refuses a correction-diff review on its own). There is no full-review rerun. A singleton batch is reserved for a substantial independent delivery or urgent isolated risk, not each item's completion by default.
+- **Correction follow-ups:** each requires a new committed correction, current deterministic evidence and the exact range `immediately-previous-reviewed-commit..new-candidate`. Continue only to resolve that batch's findings and direct regressions from the correction; stop at PASS or at an explicit PO decision. Each round must still be a real, committed correction reviewed as a diff from the immediately previous reviewed candidate; this is no authorization to repeat a review without a new correction, and it removes no course gate (a full request after round 1 stays refused).
 - **Correction-only scope:** every follow-up after the initial review examines only that immediate correction diff, including its fixes and direct regressions. Read unchanged direct contracts only as needed to judge changed behavior. Never reopen unchanged cleared areas, repeat a full current-artifact hunt, reset the base to an older review, or rename/split the same rework into a new initial round. A separately authorized material scope change is recorded separately; it cannot erase this package's lineage or grant another whole-artifact hunt over its unchanged sources.
 - **Coverage and honesty:** the coordinator retains immutable real results, receipt digests, candidate commit/tree identities, exact consecutive ranges, source path/blob/digest/mode bindings and finding dispositions. Carry forward only coverage of unchanged sources with equality proof, excluding unresolved findings until a later correction review clears them; a FAIL is never relabeled PASS. The latest actual diff PASS plus that complete verified lineage may satisfy the package's PASS contract. It is not a receipt claiming that the latest reviewer re-read every original source. Missing or ambiguous coverage leaves the package pending; it does not authorize a broad fallback review. Prior verdict prose and findings stay coordinator-side, never in the fresh Critic's input.
 - **Verification:** before the first item dispatch, the Elephant declares meaningful batch membership and intended integrated scope; after integration and before Critic, freeze actual members and integrated scope. Item completion does not automatically trigger Critic. Record every round and exact range in continuous lineage; changing batch/task/item names does not reset the budget. Self-verification, unsupported carried coverage, a gap in the chain, or an unchanged-source hunt cannot become PASS. Independent Critics remain fresh and read-only.
